# Overview
#
# A phrasal verb is a verb plus a short word such as `up`, `out`, or
# `off` that together act as one verb (`set up`, `look up`). This tier
# reports `set up`, `clean up`, `show up`, and `turn into`. `set up`
# covers install, configure, and create, so the reader cannot tell which
# one the sentence means. The fix writes one verb that says which
# (`configure the remote`). `clean up` becomes delete or remove, `show
# up` becomes appear, and `turn into` becomes become. The rule sits at
# Optional, because docs use these four often, and each mostly reads one
# way.
#
# Expression
#
# Each verb lists its forms by hand.
#
# False Positives
#
# The nouns `setup` and `cleanup` are one word and pass.
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Recommended ProsePhrasalVerb holds the idioms.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 224 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 16 of 20 sampled
# hits were a verb that one plain verb replaces. Two misfires were the
# noun `cleanup` written as two words (`the clean up of resources`). The
# other two quoted a name, the title of a linked article and the label
# of a heading in a web console.
expr main [([set, sets, setting] up), ([clean, cleans, cleaned, cleaning] up), ([show, shows, showed, shown, showing] up), ([turn, turns, turned, turning] into)]
let message "Phrasal verb. Use one verb, such as `configure`, `delete`, `appear`, or `become`."
let description "Flags `set up`, `clean up`, `show up`, and `turn into`, which one plain verb often replaces."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The setup script installs the hooks."
allows "The cleanup job deletes old builds."
